    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 while fixing WI-bivin-ronup-kuzam-giliz-sinoz-gihug-tigas-rovom (branch jgstern-agent/fix/bivin, not merged).\n\nThe bivin branch checks a BARE name against _go_names_bound_in (the names bound anywhere in the enclosing top-level declaration) BEFORE resolving it, because Go's function scope precedes the package's: a local closure or parameter named like a package function is the local value. The bound set is position-insensitive by design (its docstring: it \"over-approximates ... can only withhold an edge\"). That over-approximation now withholds a correct edge in one common Go idiom, the right-hand side of the statement that declares the shadowing name:\n\n    nodeName, err := nodeName(o)        // RHS nodeName is the PACKAGE function\n    podLabels := podLabels(ch)\n\nGo scope: a short-variable-declared name is in scope from the END of its ConstSpec/VarSpec/ShortVarDecl, so the RHS call is the package-level function. Measured over 8 repos (analyze_go, dev 7a645c6c76 vs bivin; record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/bivin/): of 1,739 previously-resolved bare sites the branch silences, 20 match NAME (, ...)? := ... NAME( on the call's own line -- alertmanager 1, beads 0, coredns 1, prometheus 7, git-bug 1, jaeger 1, cert-manager 9, runc 0. Those 20 were correct binds on dev. (The regex counts only same-line spellings; a multi-line RHS is not counted.)\n\nFIX SHAPE (not built): make the bound check position-aware for the binding statement itself -- a name bound ONLY by the short_var_declaration / var_spec whose value side contains the call is not yet bound at the call. Needs per-name binding counts per declaration rather than a set, or a scope walk.\n\nNOT CHECKED: sibling-block over-withholding (a name bound in one if-block, called bare in another), which _go_names_bound_in also over-approximates."  # 459f
    fields: {}  # 459f
